<div class="wrap narrow prose about-intro">
  <p class="lede-sm">We started <%= config.siteName %> because buying a mine in Zimbabwe shouldn't mean sorting through hundreds of forwarded messages and hoping for the best.</p>
</div>
<div class="wrap narrow prose">
  <p>Good properties are out there. Gold oxides on the Midlands belts, lumpy chrome along the Great Dyke, lithium pegmatites around Bikita and Shangani. The trouble is that information about them tends to move by word of mouth, with prices and grades that change every time the message is passed on.</p>
  <p>So we keep it simple. We work with owners and people who hold a genuine mandate. We ask to see what they've got, and we write each listing in plain language. If something is missing, like a geological report, an EIA or recent assays, we say so up front. You'd find out on the site visit anyway, and we'd rather you trusted us.</p>
  <h2>What we do</h2>
  <ul class="ticks">
    <li>Review every listing by hand before it's published</li>
    <li>Answer buyer questions and arrange site visits and sampling</li>
    <li>Pass serious offers to owners and help both sides get to a signed agreement</li>
    <li>Point you to independent geologists, assay labs and lawyers when you need them</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>What we don't do</h2>
  <p>We don't hold money and we don't guarantee grades. We aren't a substitute for your own due diligence either. Always verify title with the Ministry of Mines and Mining Development and take your own samples. We'll help you do that.</p>
  <p><a class="btn" href="/contact">Say hello</a></p>
</div>
<%- include('partials/footer') %>
